WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.036
NARRATOR: Deep beneath the
surface of the Zambezi River

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:06.172
in Zimbabwe, Africa,
Kristen Yaldor

00:00:06.239 --> 00:00:09.843
is trapped in the jaws
of a hippopotamus.

00:00:09.909 --> 00:00:11.478
As she struggles
to free herself,

00:00:11.544 --> 00:00:15.682
the animal refuses to let go,
rag-dolling her back and forth.

00:00:15.749 --> 00:00:19.052
Hippos wouldn't necessarily
just drag their victims

00:00:19.119 --> 00:00:20.353
underwater like a crocodile.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:22.155
They're not predatory species.

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:23.423
They actually just eat grass.

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:26.693
So when Kristen got
dragged underwater,

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:29.662
it's likely that the hippo
was actually just returning

00:00:29.729 --> 00:00:32.866
to where it's comfortable,
underwater, where it knew

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:34.968
that it had the
advantage to make sure

00:00:35.034 --> 00:00:36.936
that it eliminated
any threat that it

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.806
felt from Kristen's canoe.

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:43.176
I was almost out of air, and
I started to re-swallow my air,

00:00:43.243 --> 00:00:47.480
knowing that might help me
conserve my air in staying calm

00:00:47.547 --> 00:00:50.383
and allowing me to try to
survive in this moment,

00:00:50.450 --> 00:00:52.585
because I didn't know how
long this was going to last.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:55.822
The hippo can hold its breath
for two, three, five minutes.

00:00:55.889 --> 00:00:58.925
Kristen, being shook around,
probably doesn't have much

00:00:58.992 --> 00:01:00.860
more than 30 seconds of air.

00:01:00.927 --> 00:01:04.697
And so he's likely going
to last longer than she is.

00:01:04.764 --> 00:01:06.299
I had to try something.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:11.738
I grabbed its mouth to try to
pry it open and didn't budge.

00:01:11.805 --> 00:01:13.506
I'm not strong
enough to do that.

00:01:13.573 --> 00:01:17.911
I instinctively then just curled
up to try to conserve my breath

00:01:17.977 --> 00:01:20.980
and not be thrown around
so much underwater.

00:01:21.047 --> 00:01:22.382
And somehow, it let me go.

00:01:22.449 --> 00:01:23.783
DR. CAMILLE FRITSCH:
It's possible

00:01:23.850 --> 00:01:26.686
that when Kristin grabbed
on to the hippo's snout,

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.389
it actually got spooked and
let go of her, because there's

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:34.227
very few animals that a hippo
would have bit onto that would

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.196
have had the same reaction.

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:39.833
And it's possible that
actually saved her life.

00:01:39.899 --> 00:01:41.134
Kristen!

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:44.003
So what seemed like
forever, I'm standing

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:46.206
there screaming in a panic.

00:01:46.272 --> 00:01:50.176
And all of a sudden, Kristen
does pop to the surface.

00:01:50.243 --> 00:01:53.179
I immediately saw Ryan
running on the shoreline

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:55.381
with a terrified
look in his face.

00:01:55.448 --> 00:01:58.918
I immediately started to paddle
towards Ryan and the guides,

00:01:58.985 --> 00:02:00.220
but I couldn't swim.

00:02:00.286 --> 00:02:01.488
My leg wouldn't work.

00:02:01.554 --> 00:02:04.257
I screamed for help and
somehow I instinctively

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:06.659
turned over and backstroked.

00:02:06.726 --> 00:02:11.097
Drifting downriver on her
back, stroking with her arms,

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.632
trying to push herself.

00:02:12.699 --> 00:02:16.836
So at this point, I'm like,
could this hippo come back?

00:02:16.903 --> 00:02:18.471
Is there a crocodile up river?

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:22.175
Was whatever I needed to do
to get over there to help

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:24.077
the guides get her
out of the river

00:02:24.143 --> 00:02:26.813
so that the water
just didn't carry her

00:02:26.880 --> 00:02:29.182
continually towards the falls.

00:02:29.249 --> 00:02:31.784
You know, that's where
this river is going is,

00:02:31.851 --> 00:02:33.219
is over the Victoria Falls.

00:02:33.286 --> 00:02:36.089
As she passes us,
there's nobody around.

00:02:36.155 --> 00:02:37.524
I couldn't hear anything.

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.592
I was just focused on myself
trying to get to shore.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:42.896
And then I heard the guide say,
reach for the canoe paddle.

00:02:42.962 --> 00:02:44.063
[sobbing]

00:02:46.666 --> 00:02:48.735
NARRATOR: Ryan and a
guide pull Kristen ashore,

00:02:48.801 --> 00:02:51.204
where they get a clear
look at the massive damage

00:02:51.271 --> 00:02:52.739
the hippo did to her leg.

00:02:52.805 --> 00:02:55.708
When I look down, I could
see that my leg was torn open.

00:02:55.775 --> 00:03:00.179
My skin was ripped off
of my leg and is laying

00:03:00.246 --> 00:03:03.383
on the side of my leg, and I
could see part of my muscle

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.818
that was torn off sitting
on top of my thigh.

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:08.555
Hippos have these incredible
weapons in their mouths,

00:03:08.621 --> 00:03:10.990
where they have these
two canine tusks

00:03:11.057 --> 00:03:13.459
the size of a flexed human arm.

00:03:13.526 --> 00:03:15.562
But they don't actually
use them to eat.

00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:18.831
What they use the teeth for
is to defend their territories

00:03:18.898 --> 00:03:23.002
and to attack other
territorial males.

00:03:23.069 --> 00:03:25.872
Kristen, at this
point, is repeating--

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:27.640
I need help
before I bleed out.

00:03:27.707 --> 00:03:30.643
I knew I had limited time
if I was bleeding out.

00:03:30.710 --> 00:03:35.181
So my panic and my
instructions to the guides

00:03:35.248 --> 00:03:38.151
were I needed help
immediately, otherwise

00:03:38.217 --> 00:03:40.687
I was going to die here.

